  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm and dry today. Showers possible tonight and \nTuesday. \n\nWeak shortwave trough moving through the flow aloft is producing \nsome light showers or sprinkles across Ohio. This system will \nvirtually have little to no impact on our area other than the \nintroduction of some mid/high cloudiness. \n\nOtherwise...mild and mainly dry weather again today as high pressure \nalong the Mid Atlantic coastline will continue to influence the \neastern Great Lakes. Highs will be found in the 60s to low 70s in \nthe warmest spots.  \n\nA deep mid-level trough and complex elongated surface low over the \nMidwest will nudge its warm frontal segment through the region. Weak \nisentropic lift and increasing moisture will support scattered \nshowers across western NY tonight through Tuesday morning, and \nacross north-central NY late Tuesday morning through Tuesday \nafternoon. That said...the best chances will remain to our west and \nnorth-northwest. This is where the best forcing associated with the \nLLJ will be found. \n\nOtherwise...another warm day will be on tap Tuesday with Max T's \nwill again peak in the 60s to low 70s. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Unseasonably mild Wednesday, unsettled weather \nreturns Thursday. \n\nA deep southerly flow behind the front will pump in a much milder \nairmass Tuesday night into Wednesday. This will send H850 T's up to \n+13C to +15C. This will support Max T's solidly in the 70s, with \nsome locales potentially nearing 80F.  \n\nA deep mid-level trough and low over the Midwest will move to \neastern Canada late in the work week. Deep southerly flow will \ntransport moisture from the Gulf northward along the approaching \ncold front to our west. Forcing along the front interacting with a \nwealth of moisture will support medium to high confidence for \nshowers Wednesday night into Thursday. This will provide some relief \nto the recent dry spell, however confidence in rainfall amounts \nremains on the low side. Cooler air will build into the region from \nwest to east on Thursday, however it will remain warm especially \nfrom the Finger Lakes region into north-central NY. Cooler weather, \nalthough still above normal is expected Friday into the weekend.",
